Description: Midnight self-hostable Railway-style PaaS — alpha
 Midnight is an open-source application platform that targets parity with
 Railway's "deploy from a repo, get an HTTPS subdomain" workflow on a
 single Ubuntu 24.04 / Debian 12 host.
 .
 This package installs the control plane (midnight-server, midnight-worker),
 the host agent (midnight-agent), and Midnight's wrapper units for BuildKit
 (midnight-buildkit) and the OCI registry (midnight-registry). The BuildKit
 daemon and registry executable are external pinned binaries configured in
 /etc/midnight/midnight.env; distro packages are suggested for operators who
 intentionally override those paths. All six units are disabled by default;
 the operator enables them after `midnight doctor` reports green.
 The package also installs the offline `midnight-recovery` backup and disaster
 restore utility; it is not a systemd service.
 .
 Phase 0 / Phase 1 alpha. Not for public-internet production workloads.
 The supported upgrade window is encoded in the Depends/Breaks fields:
 skip-version upgrades are refused by `midnight upgrade-plan`.
